  "Question": "What is the hypothesis of the proposition “If two angles are vertically opposite angles, then the two angles are equal”?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The two angles are vertically opposite angles.",
    "B": "The two angles are equal.",
    "C": "Vertically opposite angles.",
    "D": "Equal angles."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The part after “if” is the hypothesis, and the part after “then” is the conclusion. Therefore, the hypothesis is “two angles are vertically opposite angles.”",
